    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Every so often a caravan follows a strange light off the road and doesn't come back. A few of those caravans find their way into the Feywild, and some of them decide they like it there.</p><p>Living among the fey changes a Fenari faster than any other host. Within a generation or two they shrink, their colors turn vivid and impossible (sunset orange, sea-glass blue, lilac fur with silver tips), and a pair of gossamer wings sprouts from their shoulders. Fairy Fenari soon learn the fey habits of trading in riddles, favors, and very carefully worded promises, along with a few of the fey's tricks for being seen only when they want to be.</p><p>When they return to the mortal world, Fairy Fenari make for delightful and slightly alarming traveling companions: endlessly curious, quick to fly off after anything shiny, and absolutely certain that the rules don't apply to them. They tend toward chaotic neutral.</p><p><strong>Size.</strong> Living among the fey has made these Fenari smaller than their kin, most growing between 3'4\" and 4'2\" tall and weighing 40 to 60 pounds. Your size is Small.</p><p><strong>Languages.</strong> Most Fairy Fenari learn Sylvan.</p><h3>Fairy Culture Traits</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Traits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Fairy Flight, <em>Minor Illusion</em></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><em>Faerie Fire</em></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><em>Invisibility</em></td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Spellcasting.</strong> Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells (choose when you select this Culture). You can cast each leveled spell once without a spell slot, regaining the ability when you finish a Long Rest; you can also cast them using any spell slots you have.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
